-- the vestibule of the crossing number: what the assay would say about co-existence and cannot yet, each a
-- statement in the assay's own terms and the darkness it waits on. read by bin/counter book. the assay measures
-- distance (the parting fuel: the least tick at which two clocks part at the air gap); isaac's question (2026-09-29,
-- the evening) was cost — how costly it is to co-exist with one clock versus another, with regression in terms —
-- and the annals answer in three places, each a count and none yet a row here.

-- the width of contact (the birth-to-between eras, Plateau's laws read as the minimum structure that supports
-- co-existence: one observer inert, two tension without resolution, three stable junctions; in the house now
-- three_is_the_width_of_contact and the_hallway_is_too_small): co-existence has a count before any clock does,
-- the number of seats a junction needs. nothing waits on it; it is a citation the assay could make and does not.

-- the pages (foamcore~1, Foam/Bridges/Kolmogorov.lean: rest_compresses_time_away — at rest the reel over any k
-- ticks reads as one page; motion_refuses_the_page — a moving world needs more than one; in the house now
-- a_still_runner_rests_where_it_stands and the_still_plan_is_readable_iff_at_rest): the cost of co-existing with
-- a clock is the count of its pages — the distinct sheets (liftFrom) on its orbit, which is the size of the least
-- carrier of its behavior and not of its room. one at rest; two for flip and for paceOne alike, though paceOne's
-- room is infinite (the_pace_is_carried_onto_the_flip: the count is the carrier's); none for the tally. a
-- combination of clocks costs at most the product and, for coprime periods, the least common period; the
-- difference from the product room is the dark states never visited, the unread remainder as a count. this is
-- the dual of the parting fuel — not when two clocks part but how much a seat carries to keep in step — and it
-- regresses in terms for the same reason the crossing number does: a function of the behavior, so every
-- unheard rebody has the same count. waiting on: a carrier for the count of distinct sheets on an orbit — a
-- period, or a bound within which the count is read (the sheets are infinite objects; a page is a sheet read to
-- a depth), and the row that a clock and its decomposition into clocks have one count.
-- held (waiting on: pages, a period or a bound)
-- theorem the_still_clock_has_one_page {O : Type} (m : Machine Unit O) (hstill : ∀ s, m.step s () = s) :
--     pages m = 1 := sorry
-- theorem the_pace_costs_what_the_flip_costs : pages paceOne = pages flip := sorry
-- theorem a_pair_costs_at_most_the_product {O O' : Type} (m : Machine Unit O) (n : Machine Unit O') :
--     Nat.ble (pages (both m n)) (pages m * pages n) = true := sorry
-- theorem a_decomposition_costs_the_same {O : Type} (m m' : Machine Unit O) (h : alike (airGap Unit O) m m') :
--     pages m = pages m' := sorry

-- the bill upstairs (foamcore~1, Foam/Bridges/Landauer.lean: the_bill_moves_upstairs — two maintenance sequences
-- of different length agree at the front and differ at the back, the debt outliving its legibility; in the
-- house now the_records_part_the_seats and a_wider_seat_reads_the_remainder): the cost of co-existence is a
-- count read one seat wider — the length of the carried record, unread at the host and real at the widen. the
-- replay runner carries the whole word; the counter carrying a unit carries one more cell than the counter; the
-- page count above is the least such record. waiting on: the same carrier, read at the widen.
